---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StopShield from '../components/illus/StopShield.astro';
import RScale from '../components/illus/RScale.astro';
import Horizon from '../components/illus/Horizon.astro';
import Distribution from '../components/illus/Distribution.astro';
import LayoutMosaic from '../components/illus/LayoutMosaic.astro';
import RCalendar from '../components/illus/RCalendar.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Features"
  description="FixedR's six core mechanics: mandatory stop-loss, position size from risk, R-only display, multi-account distribution, multi-monitor layouts, R calendar."
>
  <h1>Features</h1>
  <p style="max-width: 42rem; color: var(--muted);">
    Six mechanics, one idea applied consistently: risk is decided once, before the trade —
    and nothing on the screen renegotiates it with you afterwards.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-row">
    <div class="illu-box"><StopShield /></div>
    <div>
      <h2>Mandatory stop-loss</h2>
      <p>
        In FixedR there is no such thing as a position without a stop. The stop is not a
        suggestion or a habit — it is structurally required before an order exists. That single
        constraint turns "risk management" from a resolution into a property of the software.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row flip">
    <div class="illu-box"><RScale /></div>
    <div>
      <h2>Position size from risk</h2>
      <p>
        You choose what fraction of the account one R means. FixedR combines it with your stop
        distance and computes the lot size — instead of you choosing a lot size and discovering
        your risk afterwards. Same risk per trade, every trade, regardless of instrument or
        stop width.
      </p>
      <p>
        And honestly: futures contracts are discrete, so the computed size rarely matches your
        target risk exactly. FixedR rounds conservatively and shows you the <em>effective</em>
        risk next to the planned one, instead of pretending the numbers came out even. If even
        the smallest size is too large for your risk budget, it tells you the trade doesn't fit
        your profile — which is the whole philosophy in one sentence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row">
    <div class="illu-box"><Horizon /></div>
    <div>
      <h2>R-only display</h2>
      <p>
        Open positions, closed results, daily totals, drawdown headroom — everything is
        denominated in R. There is no money mode and no toggle to peek. The absence is the
        feature: what isn't rendered can't trigger you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row flip">
    <div class="illu-box"><Distribution /></div>
    <div>
      <h2>One trade, many accounts</h2>
      <p>
        Trading several funded accounts means executing the same idea several times. In FixedR
        you place the trade once and it is distributed to your accounts according to your
        configuration. And a hard promise: <strong>without configuration, nothing is guessed</strong> —
        an unconfigured account stops the distribution with a loud error instead of silently
        doing something almost right.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row">
    <div class="illu-box"><LayoutMosaic /></div>
    <div>
      <h2>Multi-monitor layouts</h2>
      <p>
        A cockpit is an arrangement of instruments, each in its fixed place. FixedR lets you
        compose charts, journal, risk panel and account views across monitors and save the
        arrangement — so that during the session, your eyes travel, not your windows.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row flip">
    <div class="illu-box"><RCalendar /></div>
    <div>
      <h2>The R calendar</h2>
      <p>
        Your trading month as a calendar of R values. Because R is stable across account sizes,
        the calendar stays comparable as you scale — a discipline record, not a money diary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="callout" style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <p style="margin: 0.4rem 0;">
      FixedR is a Windows application, works with MetaTrader &amp; NinjaTrader, and is built
      exclusively for prop-firm accounts. <a href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

